WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.520
Pasted into a chat, Markdown is a wall of symbols.

00:00:04.672 --> 00:00:06.552
Published on Markdrop, it's a page.

00:00:09.477 --> 00:00:11.457
Here's how publishing a document works.

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:16.169
Open markdrop.in/new, and write or paste.

00:00:16.902 --> 00:00:20.982
Split view shows the page as readers will see it, and scrolls with your text.

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:28.389
Until you publish, a draft stays on this device, so closing the tab doesn't lose your work.

00:00:30.631 --> 00:00:32.531
A Mermaid block becomes a diagram.

00:00:33.543 --> 00:00:36.922
Math between dollar signs is typeset with KaTeX.

00:00:37.522 --> 00:00:39.742
Code gets highlighting and a copy button.

00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:44.829
The chips above the editor say how it's published.

00:00:45.507 --> 00:00:47.187
Give the link a name, then publish.

00:00:49.963 --> 00:00:50.943
You don't need an account.

00:00:51.743 --> 00:00:53.463
Without one, you get an edit secret.

00:00:54.123 --> 00:00:57.023
Keep it, and you can edit or delete the document later.

00:00:59.498 --> 00:01:00.718
Paste the link anywhere.

00:01:01.542 --> 00:01:05.342
The preview card shows the title, the first lines, and a reading time.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.667
Readers get a clean page on any screen.

00:01:10.401 --> 00:01:13.341
They can copy a link to any heading, or export a PDF.

00:01:16.029 --> 00:01:16.749
Need a change?

00:01:17.029 --> 00:01:17.769
Edit, and save.

00:01:20.249 --> 00:01:23.749
Anyone with the page open sees it update, at the same link.

00:01:26.269 --> 00:01:30.160
Try it, no account needed, at markdrop.in/new.
